    <div class="about-copy">
      <p class="lead">Hi, I’m Pravan—a computational materials scientist who has always needed somewhere for the less measurable parts of life.</p>
      <p>When I’m not building models of materials, I’m usually making something else: a poem, a photograph, a sketch, or a stop-motion world assembled from LEGO bricks. I have written a poetry collection called <em>Words of a Thinkaholic</em>, spent many nights photographing miniatures under a desk lamp, and taught myself Blender to bring small universes to life.</p>
      <p>This site is my expressive release: a home for experiments, curiosities, half-finished ideas, and work made for the pleasure of making it. I like stories that blur boundaries—between art and analysis, order and chaos, imagination and truth.</p>
      <p>If any of it resonates, stay for a while. If you want the serious scientific side, my <a href="https://pravanop.github.io/pravan-professional-website/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">professional portfolio <i class="fa-solid fa-arrow-up-right-from-square" aria-hidden="true"></i></a> is one door away.</p>
    </div>
